  "bodyHtml": "<div class=\"notice notice-info\" role=\"note\"><strong>How this comparison was made:</strong> criteria are stated up front and every figure is drawn from the manufacturer documentation or expert sources listed at the bottom of the page. We have not yet bench-tested these products ourselves — this is a specification and documentation comparison, and it says so wherever judgment is involved. Criteria: moisture and oxygen barrier, cost per stored unit, resealability and daily-use ergonomics, durability and light protection, fitness for cottage retail.</div><p>Extension guidance names three legitimate homes for freeze-dried food: mylar bags,\nvacuum-sealed mason jars, and PETE containers, all with oxygen absorbers, all\nhermetically sealed. They are not interchangeable. Here’s how they compare on the\ncriteria that decide the choice, and which to use for what.</p>\n<figure class=\"diagram-figure\"><div class=\"table-scroll\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 920 760\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"sc-title sc-desc\">\n  <title id=\"sc-title\">Storage comparison: mylar bags, mason jars, and PETE bottles for freeze-dried food</title>\n  <desc id=\"sc-desc\">Three-column comparison. Mylar with oxygen absorber: excellent oxygen, light, and moisture barriers, decades-class shelf life, best for long-term staples. Mason jar with oxygen absorber: great oxygen barrier while sealed, no light barrier, years of storage if kept dark, best for kitchen rotation. PETE bottle with oxygen absorber: good oxygen barrier, no light barrier, months to a few years, best for staples eaten monthly.</desc>\n  <style>\n    .bg{fill:var(--sp-paper);}\n    .panel{fill:var(--sp-panel);stroke:var(--sp-line);stroke-width:1;}\n    .title{font:700 23px var(--sp-font-display);fill:var(--sp-ink);}\n    .sub{font:13px var(--sp-font-body);fill:var(--sp-ink2);}\n    .name{font:700 16px var(--sp-font-body);fill:var(--sp-ink);}\n    .tag{font:600 11.5px var(--sp-font-body);fill:var(--sp-ink3);}\n    .rl{font:700 9.5px var(--sp-font-body);fill:var(--sp-ink3);letter-spacing:0.8px;}\n    .rv{font:12px var(--sp-font-body);fill:var(--sp-ink2);}\n    .cap{font:11.5px var(--sp-font-body);fill:var(--sp-ink3);}\n    .dot-on{fill:var(--sp-ink2);}\n    .dot-off{fill:none;stroke:var(--sp-line2);stroke-width:1.2;}\n    .o2{font:700 9px var(--sp-font-body);fill:var(--sp-ink2);}\n  </style>\n\n  <rect class=\"bg\" width=\"920\" height=\"760\"/>\n\n  <text class=\"title\" x=\"24\" y=\"42\">Mylar vs. mason jars vs. PETE — what each seal is for</text>\n  <text class=\"sub\" x=\"24\" y=\"66\">All three depend on the same thing: an oxygen absorber sized to the headspace, sealed the day the batch passes the dryness test.</text>\n\n  <!-- ============ COLUMN 1: MYLAR ============ -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(24,92)\">\n    <rect class=\"panel\" width=\"276\" height=\"580\" rx=\"10\"/>\n    <!-- pouch illustration -->\n    <g>\n      <rect x=\"92\" y=\"38\" width=\"96\" height=\"106\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#DDD8CE\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <rect x=\"92\" y=\"38\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#C6BFB1\"/>\n      <path d=\"M96 57 l7 4 l7 -4 l7 4 l7 -4 l7 4 l7 -4 l7 4 l7 -4 l7 4 l7 -4 l7 4 l7 -4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--sp-ink3)\" stroke-width=\"1\" opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n      <path d=\"M104 50 L168 132\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"10\" opacity=\"0.35\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n      <rect x=\"196\" y=\"112\" width=\"42\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"var(--sp-panel)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/>\n      <text class=\"o2\" x=\"217\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O₂ 300cc</text>\n    </g>\n    <text class=\"name\" x=\"138\" y=\"184\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mylar + O₂ absorber</text>\n    <text class=\"tag\" x=\"138\" y=\"202\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the long-term vault</text>\n    <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"214\" x2=\"256\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line)\"/>\n\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,228)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">OXYGEN BARRIER</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">excellent — foil is airtight</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,278)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">LIGHT BARRIER</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">total blackout</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,328)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">MOISTURE BARRIER</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">excellent — 5+ mil foil</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,378)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">SHELF-LIFE CLASS</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">longest — decades-class, sealed</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,428)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">COST</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">low per bag; one-way seal</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,478)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">RESEALABLE</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">cut open, re-seal shorter</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,528)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">BEST FOR</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\" style=\"font-weight:600;fill:var(--sp-ink);\">long-term staples, sale inventory,</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"44\" style=\"font-weight:600;fill:var(--sp-ink);\">anything light-sensitive</text>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- ============ COLUMN 2: MASON JAR ============ -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(322,92)\">\n    <rect class=\"panel\" width=\"276\" height=\"580\" rx=\"10\"/>\n    <!-- jar illustration -->\n    <g>\n      <rect x=\"106\" y=\"30\" width=\"64\" height=\"9\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#C6BFB1\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\"/>\n      <rect x=\"100\" y=\"39\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#DDD8CE\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\"/>\n      <rect x=\"104\" y=\"58\" width=\"68\" height=\"88\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"var(--sp-frost)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"118\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"128\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"156\" cy=\"116\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"132\" cy=\"106\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"138\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"138\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <rect x=\"118\" y=\"70\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"var(--sp-panel)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/>\n      <text class=\"o2\" x=\"135\" y=\"82\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O₂</text>\n      <path d=\"M112 66 L112 132\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"5\" opacity=\"0.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    </g>\n    <text class=\"name\" x=\"138\" y=\"184\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mason jar + O₂ absorber</text>\n    <text class=\"tag\" x=\"138\" y=\"202\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the daily workhorse</text>\n    <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"214\" x2=\"256\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line)\"/>\n\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,228)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">OXYGEN BARRIER</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">great — while the lid seal holds</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,278)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">LIGHT BARRIER</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">none — glass needs a dark shelf</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,328)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">MOISTURE BARRIER</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">excellent — glass is inert</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,378)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">SHELF-LIFE CLASS</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">years — dark, cool, seal checked</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,428)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">COST</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">highest up front, reusable for life</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,478)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">RESEALABLE</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">yes — open and re-seal freely</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,528)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">BEST FOR</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\" style=\"font-weight:600;fill:var(--sp-ink);\">kitchen rotation, market display,</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"44\" style=\"font-weight:600;fill:var(--sp-ink);\">anything you open weekly</text>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- ============ COLUMN 3: PETE ============ -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(620,92)\">\n    <rect class=\"panel\" width=\"276\" height=\"580\" rx=\"10\"/>\n    <!-- bottle illustration -->\n    <g>\n      <rect x=\"126\" y=\"28\" width=\"24\" height=\"11\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#C6BFB1\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\"/>\n      <rect x=\"130\" y=\"39\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" fill=\"var(--sp-frost)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\"/>\n      <path d=\"M130 51 q-20 10 -20 30 L110 132 q0 14 14 14 L152 146 q14 0 14 -14 L166 81 q0 -20 -20 -30 z\" fill=\"var(--sp-frost)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"112\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"144\" cy=\"120\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"134\" cy=\"132\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <circle cx=\"152\" cy=\"134\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--sp-gold-t)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n      <rect x=\"124\" y=\"86\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"var(--sp-panel)\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line2)\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/>\n      <text class=\"o2\" x=\"139\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O₂</text>\n      <path d=\"M116 70 L116 130\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"5\" opacity=\"0.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    </g>\n    <text class=\"name\" x=\"138\" y=\"184\" text-anchor=\"middle\">PETE bottle + O₂ absorber</text>\n    <text class=\"tag\" x=\"138\" y=\"202\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the short-term rotator</text>\n    <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"214\" x2=\"256\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"var(--sp-line)\"/>\n\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,228)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">OXYGEN BARRIER</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">good — not foil-good</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,278)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">LIGHT BARRIER</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">clear plastic — none</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,328)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">MOISTURE BARRIER</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">very good with a tight cap</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,378)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">SHELF-LIFE CLASS</text>\n      <g><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"204\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-on\" cx=\"217\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"230\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"243\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/><circle class=\"dot-off\" cx=\"256\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.5\"/></g>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">shortest — plan to rotate through</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,428)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">COST</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">cheap, reusable, easy to source</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,478)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">RESEALABLE</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\">yes — screw cap</text>\n    </g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(0,528)\">\n      <text class=\"rl\" x=\"20\" y=\"10\">BEST FOR</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"28\" style=\"font-weight:600;fill:var(--sp-ink);\">staples you eat monthly, bulk</text>\n      <text class=\"rv\" x=\"20\" y=\"44\" style=\"font-weight:600;fill:var(--sp-ink);\">snacks, grab-and-go containers</text>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n\n  <text class=\"cap\" x=\"24\" y=\"702\">Dot ratings compare these three options against each other — the guide text below carries the sourced numbers behind them.</text>\n  <text class=\"cap\" x=\"24\" y=\"722\">None of the three works without a fresh, correctly sized oxygen absorber: the container is only as good as what you seal inside it.</text>\n</svg>\n</div><figcaption class=\"article-meta\">Comparison of mylar bags, mason jars, and PETE bottles with oxygen absorbers: barrier ratings, shelf-life class, cost, resealability, and best use for each.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"the-comparison\">The comparison</h2>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th></th><th>Mylar (5–7.5 mil, metallized)</th><th>Mason jars (vacuum-sealed)</th><th>PETE + absorber</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Moisture/O₂ barrier</td><td>Excellent when sealed correctly</td><td>Excellent (glass is a perfect barrier; lid seal is the variable)</td><td>Good, below the other two</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Light protection</td><td>Excellent (opaque)</td><td>Poor unless stored dark</td><td>Poor (usually clear)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cost per unit</td><td>Low, single-use</td><td>Higher up front, reusable for decades</td><td>Low–moderate, reusable</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Resealable in daily use</td><td>Not really (reseal shortens bag)</td><td>Yes — the everyday winner</td><td>Yes, with fresh absorbers</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Durability</td><td>Puncture is the risk; store in bins</td><td>Breakage is the risk</td><td>High</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Retail fitness</td><td>The cottage standard</td><td>Heavy, costly to sell</td><td>Rare at market</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"long-term-storage-mylar-with-discipline\">Long-term storage: mylar, with discipline</h2>\n<p>For sealed-and-forgotten storage, thick metallized mylar wins: an excellent\nmoisture, oxygen, <em>and</em> light barrier at a low per-bag cost. The qualifier is\ndiscipline, since its performance depends entirely on execution: bags in the 5–7.5 mil\nrange (not thin decorative pouches), absorbers sized around 100 cc per quart\n(300–500 cc per gallon bag), a clean wrinkle-free seal, and a next-day check that\nthe bag has drawn in slightly. Stored inside bins or buckets (mylar’s one weakness\nis puncture) below 70 °F and dark, this is the system behind every serious\nlong-term pantry.</p>\n<h2 id=\"open-and-close-pantry-use-jars\">Open-and-close pantry use: jars</h2>\n<p>Glass is a perfect barrier, and jars are the only option here that’s pleasant to\nopen weekly: vacuum-seal, use some, re-vacuum. The costs are light sensitivity\n(store dark or accept faded, degraded contents), breakage, and shelf-space\neconomics. Jars shine for the crunchy-snack rotation and powdered ingredients; they\nmake little sense for 40 pounds of long-horizon food storage.</p>\n<h2 id=\"pete-the-situational-third\">PETE: the situational third</h2>\n<p>Food-grade PETE bottles and jars with absorbers are extension-approved and durable,\nbut their barrier performance sits below mylar and glass, and they’re usually\nclear. They’re a fine home for bulk staples you’ll cycle through in a year or two,\nand a poor one for decade-scale storage of anything delicate.</p>\n<h2 id=\"for-sellers-the-answer-is-narrower\">For sellers, the answer is narrower</h2>\n<p>Cottage retail runs on printed mylar-style pouches: light, cheap to ship to you,\nattractive on a market table. Two honest caveats. First, many retail candy pouches\nare thinner than storage-grade mylar; that’s acceptable for product that sells\nwithin weeks, but label a realistic best-by window rather than borrowing “25-year”\nstorage claims from thick-mylar practice. Second, your absorber-and-seal discipline\nis now a customer-experience issue: a stale bag isn’t lost inventory, it’s a lost\nrepeat buyer. Our <a href=\"/troubleshooting/storage-failure\">storage-failure checklist</a>\ndoubles as a pre-market QA list.</p>\n<h2 id=\"bottom-line\">Bottom line</h2>\n<p>Mylar for the deep pantry, jars for the working shelf, PETE for cycled bulk, and\nretail pouches (honestly dated) for the market table. All four fail the same way:\na spent absorber or a wrinkled seal. The container matters less than the closing\nritual.</p>\n",
  "section": "Storage"
}
